          "text": "All 14 tests pass (including the `#[ignore]`d ones, run with `--include-ignored`).\n\n## Solution\n\nI implemented everything in `src/lib.rs`:\n\n- **`Luhn` struct** now stores the input as a `String` in a `digits` field.\n- **Blanket `From` impl**: `impl<T: ToString> From<T> for Luhn` — a single implementation covers `&str`, `String`, `u8`, `u16`, `u32`, `u64`, and `usize` (and any future type with `ToString`), which is the \"better solution\" hinted at in the original comment rather than hand-writing one impl per type.\n- **`is_valid`** runs the Luhn check: it walks the string from right to left, skipping whitespace, rejects any non-digit character, doubles every second digit (subtracting 9 when the result exceeds 9), and requires the digit sum to be divisible by 10 with at least two digits (so `\"0\"` and `\"1\"` are invalid).\n\nNo changes to `Cargo.toml` or the tests were needed — no external crates are required."
